@@ -201,6 +201,18 @@ You can cancel the scheduling of a group of jobs selecting them by a unique iden
 
 Will prevent every job tagged as ``daily-tasks`` from running again.
 
+To temporarily stop jobs without cancelling them, use ``schedule.pause()``
+and ``schedule.resume()``:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    schedule.pause('daily-tasks')   # run_pending() now skips these jobs
+    # ... maintenance window ...
+    schedule.resume('daily-tasks')
+
+A job whose run time passed while it was paused runs once on the first
+``run_pending()`` after resuming.
+
 
 Run a job at random intervals
